  "notes": "Boot jd_l7 from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released), navigate the service menu to T.1 SWITCH EDGES and start it, then drive each public edge separately, holding each level for 2 s: switch 43 (Outside Right Return, an ordinary rollover), 72 (Top Right Opto, a printed opto that jdGameData's inverted-switch mask normalizes), 61, 71 and 77 (printed opto-shaded cells the mask does not normalize) and 54-58 (the JUDGE drop targets, unshaded and without an opto breakout, which the mask does normalize), then the two controls again. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings the name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active. Run with --handle-mechanics 0: jd_handleMech would otherwise overwrite 77 (mech bit 0), 71 (bit 1) and 54-58 (bit 2) every frame. With it disabled the power-up test report still holds only one entry, SOUND BOARD INTERFACE ERROR, which the navigation steps through.",
